<!--
    Keeps the game's own code out of IL2CPP managed code stripping.

    Level objectives (GetMatches, GetSpecificItemMatches, DestroyObstaclesObjective, ReachBottomObjective),
    lose conditions (MoveLimit, TimeLimit) and grid converters (VerticalConvertor, HorizontalConvertor) are
    stored with [SerializeReference]. Nothing in runtime code ever constructs them; they only exist because
    Unity's deserialiser creates them from level data. That is exactly what the stripper cannot see, so at a
    higher stripping level they would be removed and every level would load with no objectives, which only
    shows up on device, never in the editor.

    The whole assembly is preserved rather than a list of those types, because a list silently breaks the
    first time a new objective or condition is added. Game code is small, so the size cost is negligible.
-->
<linker>
    <assembly fullname="Assembly-CSharp" preserve="all"/>
</linker>
